@flexiarg buffer-cleaner/kill
@title Kill With A Receipt, Never Without A Gate
@keywords kill, fuel, receipt, dry-run, gate, refusal, proposal
@audience buffer-cleaner adapter, consumer builders
@tone technical
@style pattern
@status staged (live evaluation: futon2 buffer-cleaner-adapter; execute! is a typed refusal — live kill ungated; fuel declaration: per-scan 0.01, per-kill 0.1, one unit = one nat, worked-example convention 74c298f0)
@references [buffer-cleaner/classify-staleness buffer-cleaner/yield-settled buffer-cleaner/exempt-the-in-use]
@see-also apparatus/every-wait-has-a-deadline
@why the adapter produces kill proposals in a live operator session (Joe's Emacs); an ungated kill path there is the U59 class (acting on a target whose liveness you have not verified) with no compensating mechanism yet. Receipts make every proposal auditable before any gate exists.
@how emit a typed receipt per proposed kill {buffer, kind, decisiveness, prior, revisit-cost, expected-recovery, fuel charge}; charge fuel from the declared rates; refuse execution with a typed refusal naming the missing gate until a reviewed consumer wires receipts to real kills.
@violation-signature A kill executed by anything other than the gated consumer; receipts missing the classification they were based on; fuel charged at rates that differ from the declaration.
! conclusion: The kill chip proposes with a receipt and refuses to execute ungated: proposals have receipts, acts have gates.

  + context: The cleaner runs unattended in a live editor session shared with active agents and the operator.

  + IF:
    Classification has marked buffers eligible and the wiring proposes kills.

  + HOWEVER:
    A dry run feels like half an implementation; the temptation is to wire kill-buffer directly once classification looks right. But nothing yet re-verifies liveness at execution time atomically, and the buffer-cleaner's history (the near-miss modified-file kill) shows exactly the class of error gates exist for.

  + THEN:
    Emit receipts only; keep execute! as a typed refusal (:execute-not-gated, naming the required gate); let a separately reviewed consumer own the act, carrying the receipt's provenance into any real commit.

  + BECAUSE:
    Proposal and act are different objects with different obligations (R9 at adapter grain): the first needs a record, the second needs a gate — collapsing them makes every classification bug an editor incident.

  + evidence: The corrected packet's aggressive run proposes 3 kills, all receipts carrying their classification; the scoring consumer (codex-26) consumed receipts offline with no live operation.

  + NEXT-STEPS:
    - Designing the gated consumer (atomic liveness re-verify at execution time) is prerequisite work before any live kill path — the inbox-zero compensating-safety pattern is the template.
